{{also|морѥ}}
==Bulgarian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|bg|sla-pro|*moře}}, reanalyzed as an {{m|sla-pro|*-ę}} stem, from {{inh|bg|ine-pro|*móri}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{bg-IPA|море́}}

====Noun====
{{bg-noun|море́|n}}

# [[sea]], [[briny]]
# [[seaside]]
# {{lb|bg|figuratively}} [[thousands]] of, a [[wilderness]] of, as in ''море от люде'' - ''thousands of people''

=====Declension=====
{{bg-ndecl|море́<+ета+я[<a> or <p>]>}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|bg|el|μωρέ}}, frozen vocative of {{m|el|μωρός}}, meaning [[stupid]], but commonly used as a colloquial address.

====Pronunciation====
* {{bg-IPA|мо́ре}}

====Particle====
{{head|bg|particle|head=мо́ре}}

# {{lb|bg|archaic}} [[you]], general vocative expression, used to augment an address

===References===
* {{R:RBE}}
* {{R:RBE2}}

